    "project": {
      "accession": "PXD029204",
      "title": "Protein profiles of ACUTE liver injury in mice mediated by CCl4 or APAP",
      "additionalAttributes": [],
      "projectDescription": "Mice were treated with CCl4,APAP or olive oil for 24 h, protein changes were detected by mass spectrometry",
      "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Mice were treated with CCl4,APAP or olive oil for 24 h.The mouse samples were treated with acetone precipitation, mass spectroscopy-grade trypsin digestion, and C18 stage tips (Thermo Fisher Scientific, USA) desalination. Then, samples were analyzed by using an Orbitrap Exploris 480 mass spectrometer equipped with the FAIMS Pro interface and an EASY-nanoLC system (Medical Research Center for Structural Biology, Wuhan University). EASY-nanoLC was configured with a Hypersil GOLD C18 Selectivity HPLC column. The HPLC gradient was as follows: 2% to 8% solvent B (A=0.1% formic acid in water; B=80% acetonitrile, 0.1% formic acid) in 2 min from 8% to 32% solvent B over 168 min, from 32% to 100% solvent B in 6 min, 100% solvent B for 4 min at a flow-rate of 300 nl/min. Full scan mass range was 350-1500 m/z and Obitrap resolution was 60000.",
      "dataProcessingProtocol": "Data were acquired using a data-dependent acquisition method and analyzed by Protein Discovery (Thermo Fisher Scientific, USA) using a four-stage searching program. The strict target false discovery rate (FDR) for PSMs or peptides was set at 0.01. Peptides with a lower confidence than 0.01 were excluded. For protein assembling, all proteins with a q-value higher than 0.01 received high confidence, while higher than 0.05 received medium confidence.",
